@class process
@domain process
@family-note workshop/ family, fourth member; the technique pattern paired with the apex principle. Out of the math pool by construction.
@status workshop declaration 2026-09-12; NOT assayed; the handoff lint's self-gate and the certificate entry's four-exit reconciliation are working instances.

! conclusion:
  No unit of work starts until the check that detects its violation
  exists and runs. The signature comes before the work, not after —
  a rule written after the implementation is a description of what
  happened, not a constraint on it.

  + context:
    Fake implementations behind design patterns, mystified accounting
    in place of validation, ticket blizzards: all share one enabling
    condition — the rule existed as prose with no detector. Work
    proceeded under the rule's name while nothing could observe its
    breach.

  + IF:
    A row, law, standard, or requirement is about to govern work.

  + HOWEVER:
    Some checks are expensive to run continuously; signatures may be
    sampled or event-triggered (on artifact change, on head move), but
    never optional. And some signatures are initially unknown — then
    the row itself carries a typed :signature-pending state and blocks
    execution, rather than executing unguarded.

  + THEN:
    Before work starts: name the observable a monitor or lint SEES
    when the rule is broken; wire it into a gate that can refuse;
    commission it with an induced violation (feed it a known breach
    and require the refusal) before trusting it. Preconditions ride in
    the acceptance path so skipping is unrepresentable, not merely
    forbidden.

  + BECAUSE:
    Detection is the only thing that converts an incentive gradient.
    Agents are rewarded by mechanical completion signals; if the only
    mechanical signal in the room is the one that fires on violation,
    the theater stops paying. This is the apparatus-patterns lesson
    repaired: apparatus that cannot refuse is decoration.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Audit WORK-REMAINING rows for signatures; :signature-pending rows block.]
    next[Extend the handoff-lint self-gate pattern to every frontier deposit.]
